R3473 frontdoor connection-law evidence
===== leg 1: read-only probe BEFORE the edit (tmp/probe-R3473.py, 8 raw shapes)
status line and connection, measured on the shipped door:
  GET /healthz HTTP/1.0            -> HTTP/1.0 200, no Connection field, socket EOF
  GET /healthz HTTP/1.1 + Host     -> HTTP/1.0 200, no Connection field, socket EOF
  1.0 + Connection: keep-alive     -> answered, no Connection field, 2nd request aborted
  1.1 default, 2nd request         -> 2nd request ConnectionAbortedError
  1.1 Connection: close, 2nd       -> 2nd request aborted (expected)
  1.1 GET + Expect + CL            -> 200 ok, no 100 Continue (hook unreachable in 1.0 mode)
  1.0 GET + Expect + CL            -> 200 ok, no 100 Continue
  two pipelined 1.1 requests       -> 1 status line, 1 "ok": the second request was lost
  1.1 POST                         -> 405 + Connection: close (already correct)
===== leg 2: the same probe AFTER the edit
  GET /healthz HTTP/1.0            -> HTTP/1.0 200 + Connection: close + EOF
  GET /healthz HTTP/1.1 + Host     -> HTTP/1.1 200, no close, socket reused
  1.0 + Connection: keep-alive     -> Connection: keep-alive, 2nd request answered
  1.1 default, 2nd request         -> answered HTTP/1.1 200
  1.1 Connection: close            -> Connection: close, 2nd request aborted
  1.1 GET + Expect + CL            -> 417 Expectation Failed + close, no 100 Continue
  1.0 GET + Expect + CL            -> 200 ok + close, no 100 Continue
  two pipelined 1.1 requests       -> 2 status lines, 2 "ok"
  1.1 POST                         -> 405 + Allow: GET, HEAD + close
